      "message": "For kernel 5.15+, we can use xa_for_each() following the change: \n\n\"a33df75c63 block: use an xarray for disk-\u003epart_tbl\" , which modify structure as:\n-\t/* Array of pointers to partitions indexed by partno.\n-\t * Protected with matching bdev lock but stat and other\n-\t * non-critical accesses use RCU.  Always access through\n-\t * helpers.\n-\t */\n-\tstruct disk_part_tbl __rcu *part_tbl;\n+\tstruct xarray part_tbl;\n \tstruct block_device *part0;\n\nBut our driver(eMMC/UFS write protect) can use disk_part_iter_xxx symbol instead of xa_for_each() to iterate partitions in one disk for kernel 5.10.",
